  <p><a id="homeLink" href="/">← Back to Home</a> | HTML Course - Lesson 7 / 50</p>
  <h1>Lesson 7: Forms in HTML</h1>
  <p>Learn How to Create Forms with input, label, textarea, select, radio, checkbox and button | LearnHTMLCSSJS.com</p>
</header>

<div class="container">
  <div class="tabs">
    <button id="lessonTabBtn" class="tab-btn active" onclick="showLesson()">📖 Lesson</button>
    <button id="testTabBtn" class="tab-btn" onclick="showTest()">📝 Test - 100 Marks</button>
  </div>
  <div id="lockMsg" class="lock-msg">🔒 Test is running! All tabs are locked until you submit the test or time ends.</div>

  <div id="lessonContent">
    <h2>1. What is a Form in HTML?</h2>
    <p>A form is used to <b>take information from the user</b>. For example - Login Form, Signup Form, Contact Form, Search Box.</p>
    <div class="note"><b>Example:</b> When you type your name on Facebook Signup, that is a form. When you search on Google, that is also a form.</div>
    <p>The form has 3 main parts:</p>
    <table>
      <tr><th>Tag</th><th>Meaning</th><th>Work</th></tr>
      <tr><td>&lt;form&gt;</td><td>Form</td><td>Creates the full form</td></tr>
      <tr><td>&lt;input&gt;</td><td>Input</td><td>Creates a box to type in</td></tr>
      <tr><td>&lt;label&gt;</td><td>Label</td><td>Shows text for the input box</td></tr>
    </table>
    <h2>2. Basic Form - Name + Submit</h2>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="tag">&lt;form&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;label&gt;</span><span class="text">Your Name:</span><span class="tag">&lt;/label&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;input</span> <span class="attr">type</span>=<span class="val">"text"</span> <span class="attr">placeholder</span>=<span class="val">"Enter your name"</span><span class="tag">&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;button&gt;</span><span class="text">Submit</span><span class="tag">&lt;/button&gt;</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;/form&gt;</span>
    </code></div>
    <div class="result">
      <b>Result - Try it:</b>
      <form onsubmit="return false">
        <label class="demo-label">Your Name:</label>
        <input class="demo-input" type="text" placeholder="Enter your name">
        <button class="btn" type="button">Submit</button>
      </form>
    </div>
    <h2>3. Input Types - Very Important</h2>
    <p><b>type</b> tells the browser what kind of box to show. If type is wrong, the form will not work correctly.</p>
    <table>
      <tr><th>Type</th><th>Use For</th><th>Example</th></tr>
      <tr><td>text</td><td>Name, City</td><td>Ali</td></tr>
      <tr><td>password</td><td>Password (hidden)</td><td>••••••</td></tr>
      <tr><td>email</td><td>Email Address</td><td>ali@gmail.com</td></tr>
      <tr><td>number</td><td>Age, Marks</td><td>18</td></tr>
      <tr><td>date</td><td>Date of Birth</td><td>01-01-2010</td></tr>
      <tr><td>radio</td><td>Select 1 option</td><td>Male / Female</td></tr>
      <tr><td>checkbox</td><td>Select many options</td><td>HTML, CSS</td></tr>
      <tr><td>submit</td><td>Submit Button</td><td>Submit</td></tr>
    </table>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="tag">&lt;input</span> <span class="attr">type</span>=<span class="val">"text"</span><span class="tag">&gt;</span> <span class="text">- Name</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;input</span> <span class="attr">type</span>=<span class="val">"password"</span><span class="tag">&gt;</span> <span class="text">- Password</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;input</span> <span class="attr">type</span>=<span class="val">"email"</span><span class="tag">&gt;</span> <span class="text">- Email</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;input</span> <span class="attr">type</span>=<span class="val">"number"</span><span class="tag">&gt;</span> <span class="text">- Age</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;input</span> <span class="attr">type</span>=<span class="val">"date"</span><span class="tag">&gt;</span> <span class="text">- Date</span>
    </code></div>
    <div class="result">
      <b>Result:</b>
      <form onsubmit="return false">
        <label class="demo-label">Name:</label><input class="demo-input" type="text" placeholder="Ali">
        <label class="demo-label">Password:</label><input class="demo-input" type="password" placeholder="••••••">
        <label class="demo-label">Email:</label><input class="demo-input" type="email" placeholder="ali@gmail.com">
        <label class="demo-label">Age:</label><input class="demo-input" type="number" placeholder="18">
        <label class="demo-label">Date of Birth:</label><input class="demo-input" type="date">
      </form>
    </div>
    <h2>4. placeholder and required</h2>
    <p><b>placeholder</b> = Light grey text inside the box. It tells the user what to type.<br><b>required</b> = User must fill this box. Form will not submit if it is empty.</p>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="tag">&lt;input</span> <span class="attr">type</span>=<span class="val">"text"</span> <span class="attr">placeholder</span>=<span class="val">"Enter your name"</span> <span class="attr">required</span><span class="tag">&gt;</span>
    </code></div>
    <h2>5. Radio Button - Select Only 1</h2>
    <p>Radio is used when the user can select <b>only one</b> option. All radio buttons must have the <b>same name</b>.</p>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="tag">&lt;input</span> <span class="attr">type</span>=<span class="val">"radio"</span> <span class="attr">name</span>=<span class="val">"gender"</span><span class="tag">&gt;</span><span class="text"> Male</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;input</span> <span class="attr">type</span>=<span class="val">"radio"</span> <span class="attr">name</span>=<span class="val">"gender"</span><span class="tag">&gt;</span><span class="text"> Female</span>
    </code></div>
    <div class="result"><b>Result:</b><br><label><input type="radio" name="demo-gender"> Male</label> &nbsp;<label><input type="radio" name="demo-gender"> Female</label></div>
    <h2>6. Checkbox - Select Many</h2>
    <p>Checkbox is used when the user can select <b>many</b> options.</p>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="tag">&lt;input</span> <span class="attr">type</span>=<span class="val">"checkbox"</span><span class="tag">&gt;</span><span class="text"> HTML</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;input</span> <span class="attr">type</span>=<span class="val">"checkbox"</span><span class="tag">&gt;</span><span class="text"> CSS</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;input</span> <span class="attr">type</span>=<span class="val">"checkbox"</span><span class="tag">&gt;</span><span class="text"> JavaScript</span>
    </code></div>
    <div class="result"><b>Result:</b><br><label><input type="checkbox"> HTML</label> &nbsp;<label><input type="checkbox"> CSS</label> &nbsp;<label><input type="checkbox"> JavaScript</label></div>
    <h2>7. textarea and select - Big Text and Dropdown</h2>
    <p><b>textarea</b> = Big box for long text like message or address.<br><b>select + option</b> = Dropdown list like City, Country.</p>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="tag">&lt;textarea</span> <span class="attr">rows</span>=<span class="val">"3"</span> <span class="attr">placeholder</span>=<span class="val">"Your message"</span><span class="tag">&gt;&lt;/textarea&gt;</span><br><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;select&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;option&gt;</span><span class="text">Multan</span><span class="tag">&lt;/option&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;option&gt;</span><span class="text">Lahore</span><span class="tag">&lt;/option&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;option&gt;</span><span class="text">Karachi</span><span class="tag">&lt;/option&gt;</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;/select&gt;</span>
    </code></div>
    <div class="result">
      <b>Result:</b>
      <form onsubmit="return false">
        <label class="demo-label">Your Message:</label>
        <textarea class="demo-input" rows="3" placeholder="Your message"></textarea>
        <label class="demo-label">Your City:</label>
        <select class="demo-input"><option>Multan</option><option>Lahore</option><option>Karachi</option></select>
      </form>
    </div>
    <h2>8. Full Example - Signup Form</h2>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="tag">&lt;form&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;label&gt;</span><span class="text">Name:</span><span class="tag">&lt;/label&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;input</span> <span class="attr">type</span>=<span class="val">"text"</span> <span class="attr">required</span><span class="tag">&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;label&gt;</span><span class="text">Email:</span><span class="tag">&lt;/label&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;input</span> <span class="attr">type</span>=<span class="val">"email"</span> <span class="attr">required</span><span class="tag">&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;label&gt;</span><span class="text">Password:</span><span class="tag">&lt;/label&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;input</span> <span class="attr">type</span>=<span class="val">"password"</span> <span class="attr">required</span><span class="tag">&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;button&gt;</span><span class="text">Signup</span><span class="tag">&lt;/button&gt;</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;/form&gt;</span>
    </code></div>
    <div class="result">
      <b>Result - Signup Form:</b>
      <form onsubmit="return false">
        <label class="demo-label">Name:</label><input class="demo-input" type="text" placeholder="Enter name" required>
        <label class="demo-label">Email:</label><input class="demo-input" type="email" placeholder="Enter email" required>
        <label class="demo-label">Password:</label><input class="demo-input" type="password" placeholder="Enter password" required>
        <button class="btn" type="button">Signup</button>
      </form>
    </div>
    <h2>9. Homework - Practice for 2 Minutes</h2>
    <p>Create a form with:</p>
    <p>1. <b>Text</b> input for Name<br>2. <b>Email</b> input for Email<br>3. <b>Radio</b> for Male / Female (same name)<br>4. <b>Checkbox</b> for HTML / CSS<br>5. <b>Select</b> for City<br>6. <b>Button</b> - Submit</p>
    <div class="box"><b>Remember:</b> form = Full form | input = Box | label = Text for box | type = text, password, email, number, date, radio, checkbox | placeholder = Hint text | required = Must fill | textarea = Big box | select + option = Dropdown | button = Submit</div>
    <p><b>Next Step:</b> After this lesson, go to <a href="/lesson8">Lesson 8 - Div & Span</a> to learn how to group content.</p>
    <a id="playgroundLink" class="btn" href="/playground">▶ Try it Yourself - Playground</a><br><br>
    <button class="btn btn-next" onclick="showTest()">Go to Test → 📝</button>
    <div class="nav">
      <a class="btn btn-prev" href="/lesson6">← Lesson 6</a>
      <a id="nextLessonLink" class="btn btn-next" href="/lesson8">Next Lesson 8 →</a>
    </div>
  </div>

