      <div class="test-info"><b>Total Questions:</b> 10 &nbsp; | &nbsp; <b>Total Marks:</b> 100 &nbsp; | &nbsp; <b>Passing Marks:</b> 80 (80%) &nbsp; | &nbsp; <b>Time:</b> 3 Minutes<br>Each correct answer = 10 Marks. Once you start, all tabs will be locked until you submit.</div>
      <div id="startScreen">
        <h2>Ready for the Test?</h2>
        <p>Click Start Paper to begin. You will get <b>3 Minutes</b> for 10 questions.<br>During the test, you cannot open Lesson or any other page.</p>
        <button class="btn" style="font-size:20px;padding:14px 30px" onclick="startTest()">▶ Start Paper</button>
      </div>
      <div id="timerBar">⏰ Time Left: <span id="timerText">03:00</span></div>
      <div id="quizArea">
        <form id="quizForm">
          <div class="question"><b>Q1. Which tag creates a Form?</b><label><input type="radio" name="q1" value="a"> &lt;input&gt;</label><label><input type="radio" name="q1" value="b"> &lt;form&gt;</label><label><input type="radio" name="q1" value="c"> &lt;label&gt;</label><label><input type="radio" name="q1" value="d"> &lt;button&gt;</label></div>
          <div class="question"><b>Q2. Which tag creates a box to type in?</b><label><input type="radio" name="q2" value="a"> &lt;form&gt;</label><label><input type="radio" name="q2" value="b"> &lt;input&gt;</label><label><input type="radio" name="q2" value="c"> &lt;label&gt;</label><label><input type="radio" name="q2" value="d"> &lt;textarea&gt;</label></div>
          <div class="question"><b>Q3. Which input type is used for Password (hidden)?</b><label><input type="radio" name="q3" value="a"> type="text"</label><label><input type="radio" name="q3" value="b"> type="password"</label><label><input type="radio" name="q3" value="c"> type="email"</label><label><input type="radio" name="q3" value="d"> type="hide"</label></div>
          <div class="question"><b>Q4. Which input type is used for Email?</b><label><input type="radio" name="q4" value="a"> type="text"</label><label><input type="radio" name="q4" value="b"> type="email"</label><label><input type="radio" name="q4" value="c"> type="mail"</label><label><input type="radio" name="q4" value="d"> type="number"</label></div>
          <div class="question"><b>Q5. What does placeholder do?</b><label><input type="radio" name="q5" value="a"> Shows hint text inside box</label><label><input type="radio" name="q5" value="b"> Makes box required</label><label><input type="radio" name="q5" value="c"> Hides the box</label><label><input type="radio" name="q5" value="d"> Changes box color</label></div>
          <div class="question"><b>Q6. What does required do?</b><label><input type="radio" name="q6" value="a"> User must fill the box</label><label><input type="radio" name="q6" value="b"> Box becomes hidden</label><label><input type="radio" name="q6" value="c"> Box becomes big</label><label><input type="radio" name="q6" value="d"> Nothing</label></div>
          <div class="question"><b>Q7. Radio button is used to select?</b><label><input type="radio" name="q7" value="a"> Only 1 option</label><label><input type="radio" name="q7" value="b"> Many options</label><label><input type="radio" name="q7" value="c"> No option</label><label><input type="radio" name="q7" value="d"> All options</label></div>
          <div class="question"><b>Q8. Checkbox is used to select?</b><label><input type="radio" name="q8" value="a"> Only 1 option</label><label><input type="radio" name="q8" value="b"> Many options</label><label><input type="radio" name="q8" value="c"> No option</label><label><input type="radio" name="q8" value="d"> Nothing</label></div>
          <div class="question"><b>Q9. Which tag is used for a Dropdown list?</b><label><input type="radio" name="q9" value="a"> &lt;select&gt; + &lt;option&gt;</label><label><input type="radio" name="q9" value="b"> &lt;input&gt;</label><label><input type="radio" name="q9" value="c"> &lt;textarea&gt;</label><label><input type="radio" name="q9" value="d"> &lt;dropdown&gt;</label></div>
